## QA

Executable flows. Each step carries a human instruction (`do`) and, where the step maps to an
invocable operation, an agent binding (`invoke`). Report failures by flow and step number.

```mdl
flow QA-1: Create a sheet, set values, evaluate a formula, read back
  desc: The core spreadsheet round-trip — create, set cells (including a formula), read the
    evaluated result back.
  actors: agent
  covers: [F-1.1, F-1.2, F-2.1, F-2.3, T-1, T-2]
  status: unverified
  given:
    - an identity exists
    - space: a space is open
    - root: the space's root collection — [op:create] takes no target and files the Sheet
      there via `CollectionModel.add`, so the flow cannot choose a different one
    - no Sheet named "QA Sheet" exists — ABORT rather than reusing one this flow did not create
  test:
    - name: Create the sheet
      do: In the navtree, click + on a collection and choose Sheet. Name it "QA Sheet".
      invoke: [op:create] { name: "QA Sheet" }
      capture: created
      expect: a Sheet named "QA Sheet" now exists
      assert: return !!$created.id

    - name: Place it in the root collection
      do: (no separate gesture — the navtree create action places it)
      expect: "QA Sheet" appears as a row under the space's root collection
      note: |
        NO `invoke` — [op:create] places the sheet in the space itself, so a following
        `space.addObject` is redundant. `$created.id` is a DXN string, not an object;
        resolve it (`db.getObjectById` on the DXN's last segment) before any step that
        needs the live Sheet.

    - name: Resolve the sheet and set values
      do: Click cell A1 and type "10", Enter. Click A2 and type "20", Enter. Click A3 and type
        "=A1+A2", Enter.
      invoke: [op:setRange] { sheet: space.db.makeRef($created.id), cells: { A1: 10, A2: 20, A3: "=A1+A2" } }
      expect: A1 shows 10, A2 shows 20, and A3 shows 30 (evaluated by HyperFormula)
      note: |
        `sheet` is a `Ref` and `op:create` returns only `{ id }` (a DXN string) — `db.makeRef`
        builds the `Ref` straight from that DXN, no load needed; `Ref.make` needs a live object,
        which nothing captured here has.

    - name: Read the range back
      do: (agent-only — confirm the evaluated values)
      invoke: [op:getRange] { sheet: space.db.makeRef($created.id), range: "A1:A3" }
      expect: A3 renders 30 in the grid
      assert: |
        // getRange returns STORED cell content, not the evaluated result — A3 comes back as
        // the formula string. Judge the evaluated value in the UI (`expect`), not here.
        return $result.values.flat().slice(0, 2).join(',') === '10,20';
  after:
    - name: Delete the sheet
      do: Right-click "QA Sheet" in the navtree and choose Delete.
      invoke: org.dxos.operation.space.removeObjects { objects: [space.db.getObjectById($created.id.split('/').pop())] }
      expect: the row leaves the navtree and its plank closes if it was open
      note: |
        No `target` — `op:create` calls `CollectionModel.add({ object })` with no target, so the
        Sheet lands in the space's root collection; omitting `target` here lets `removeObjects`
        default to that same collection rather than a different one.
```

